
* Diode SPICE subcircuit
* Generic diode model with proper SPICE parameters
*
* Parameters:
*   IS - Saturation current (controls forward voltage)
*   N - Ideality factor (1.0 for ideal diode, higher for real diodes)
*   RS - Series resistance
*   CJO - Junction capacitance (optional)
*
* Nodes:
*   1 - Anode
*   2 - Cathode

* Standard silicon diode - ~0.7V forward voltage
.SUBCKT D 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10m CJO=1p
D1 1 2 DMODEL
.MODEL DMODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D

* Schottky diode variant - ~0.3V forward voltage, higher leakage
.SUBCKT D_Schottky 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-8 N=1.2 RS=5m CJO=2p
D1 1 2 SCHOTTKY_MODEL
.MODEL SCHOTTKY_MODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D_Schottky

* Zener diode variant - includes breakdown behavior
.SUBCKT D_Zener 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10m BV=5.1 IBV=5m CJO=1p
D1 1 2 ZENER_MODEL
.MODEL ZENER_MODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} BV={BV} IBV={IBV} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D_Zener
XD1 V5 V5_ESP D_Schottky IS=1e-8 N=1.2 RS=5m CJO=2p


* Case A (0-10 ms): buck on (5.0 V), DevKit draws 0.12 A idle, 0.5 A Wi-Fi TX burst at 5 ms.
* Case B (10-20 ms): buck off (+5V rail = eyes/buzzer/logic, ~25 Ohm), USB powers the DevKit at 5.1 V.
V_BUCK VB GND PWL(0 5.0 10m 5.0 10.01m 0)
S_BUCK VB V5 CTRL GND SWBUCK
V_CTRL CTRL GND PWL(0 1 10m 1 10.01m 0)
.model SWBUCK SW(RON=0.02 ROFF=1e9 VT=0.5 VH=0.1)
R_RAIL V5 GND 25
V_USB VU GND PWL(0 0 10m 0 10.01m 5.1)
D_USB VU V5_ESP DUSB
.model DUSB D(IS=1e-6 N=1.05 RS=0.05)
I_ESP V5_ESP GND PWL(0 0.12 5m 0.12 5.01m 0.5 7m 0.5 7.01m 0.12)
.control
  tran 5u 20m
  meas tran vesp_idle FIND v(V5_ESP) AT=4m
  meas tran vesp_tx FIND v(V5_ESP) AT=6m
  meas tran v5rail_usb FIND v(V5) AT=19m
  let iback = v(V5)/25
  meas tran iback_usb FIND iback AT=19m
.endc
